# Conan registry version collision requires a new recipe identity
id:                     E2178-draft-2301
trigger_tool:           conan|ci|git
phase:                  pre-pr|ci|repair|version-selection
error_signature:        'version_not_incremented|already published with different recipe|cnb.cool.*409|recipe.*collision'
severity:               2
category:               conan|registry|versioning|ci|repair|evidence
match_keywords:         Conan recipe revision collision, same version published, version_not_incremented, successor version, exact branch identity, immutable failed PR
title:                  Published Conan versions require a new recipe and branch identity
root_cause:             The OHPCD CI registry gate rejects a changed recipe when the same package/version already has a published recipe because the remote does not support parallel recipe revisions for that identity. A local build PASS cannot override this registry identity conflict.
affected_scope:         Any OpenHarmony PC Conan adaptation whose package/version is already published and whose recipe or source metadata changes.
verification_cmd:       run exact-head CI; when L0 reports version_not_incremented, query the suggested successor version, create a new version directory, update recipe self.version and conandata keys, use feat/<package>-<version> branch, and bind a new Issue/PR contract.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           create-successor-version
rec_description:        Preserve the failed PR and CI receipt as immutable history. Increment only the adaptation suffix (for example X.Y.Z -> X.Y.Z.1), keep the upstream source URL/version unchanged, regenerate candidate tree and contract hashes, and submit a distinct PR with exact branch/package/version identity.
rec_command:            'freeze failed CI -> create successor directory/branch -> update recipe+manifest+test identity -> new Issue/PRE_CREATE -> new PR/POST_CREATE -> exact-head CI'
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                transaction
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      fail-closed-version
fallback_description:   If the registry collision cannot be confirmed or the platform does not accept the successor identity, stop before modifying the old PR and record the candidate as blocked; never force-push or relabel the failed version.
fallback_command:       'read authoritative CI diagnosis and registry state; preserve old PR; do not retry the same version'
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          validation
forbid_1_pattern:       retry.*same.*version|force-push.*old.*PR|reuse.*failed.*CI
forbid_1_reason:        Reusing the failed identity hides a registry collision and breaks exact-head evidence.
forbid_1_consequence:   A later CI result can be attributed to the wrong recipe/version or overwrite immutable history.
forbid_2_pattern:       change.*upstream.*version.*only.*to.*avoid.*collision|guess.*registry.*revision
forbid_2_reason:        The adaptation suffix identifies the recipe; the source release remains the upstream version unless source itself changed.
forbid_2_consequence:   Package metadata, source hash, and downstream references become inconsistent.
principles:             P001,P007,P018,P020
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E2177
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
